<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30471" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nā^trix</span></b> , īcis
		(once m.: <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">natrix violator aquae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					9, 720</span></i>
			; usually), f.
			no. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A water-snake</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cur deus tantam vim natricum viperarumque
					fecerit?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Ac. 2, 38, 120</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, of a dangerous person: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">se natricem educare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 11</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a whip,
			scourge</i>, made of a watersnake's skin: natibu' natricem
			impressit crassam et capitatam, Lucil. ap.
				<i><span class="en">Non. 65,
			30</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A plant</i>: Ononis natrix, Linn.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 27,
				12, 83, § 107</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
